## Problems in a graph.
problem-no-trigger = The graph has no trigger, such as a slash command.
problem-several-triggers = The graph has more than one trigger.
problem-unknown-node-type = Unknown node type { $type }. Is a plugin missing?
problem-unknown-pin = The wire at { $pin } leads nowhere.
problem-wrong-direction = The wire at { $pin } goes the wrong way.
problem-kind-mismatch = { $from } and { $to } cannot be wired together.
problem-several-sources = { $pin } has more than one wire.
problem-missing-prop = The field “{ $prop }” is empty.
problem-unknown-prop = The field “{ $prop }” does not belong to this node.
problem-wrong-prop-type = The field “{ $prop }” has the wrong kind of value.
problem-template-unclosed = The field “{ $prop }” has a {"{"} that is never closed.
problem-template-stray = The field “{ $prop }” has a {"}"} with no {"{"}. Write {"}}"} for a brace.
problem-template-empty = The field “{ $prop }” has an empty variable, such as {"{}"}.
problem-unknown-variable = The field “{ $prop }” uses { $path }, which does not exist.
problem-variable-type = The field “{ $prop }” uses { $path }, which is of another type.
problem-bad-number = The field “{ $prop }” must be a number above 0 and at most { $max }, or a variable.
problem-no-reply = Warning: the command can end without “Reply”, and Discord then shows “The application did not respond”.
problem-reply-in-event = “Reply” works only in commands and in “New message”. Here, use “Send to a channel”.
problem-form-field = Field { $field }: { $why }
problem-form-title = The form's title is at most 45 characters.
problem-form-count = A form has 1–5 fields.
problem-form-name = its name must be 1–32 lower-case letters, digits, - or _, used once.
problem-form-label = its label must be 1–45 characters.
problem-form-placeholder = its hint is at most 100 characters.
problem-form-length = its lengths must be 0–4000 (the maximum at least 1), the minimum not above the maximum.
problem-form-not-first = “Show form” must be the bot's first answer: right after the command or click, with only conditions before it, and alone on its wire.
problem-reply-after-closed-form = After a form nobody sent, there is nothing to reply to. Here, use “Send to a channel”.
problem-wrong-trigger = This node works only in graphs started by: { $allowed }.
problem-private-outside-command = Only a command's reply can be seen by its author alone. Switch off “Only the command author sees it”.
problem-empty-message = The message has no text and no embed title or description.
problem-bad-color = The field “{ $prop }” must be a colour like #5865F2, or a variable.
problem-no-permission-check = Warning: an action that needs “{ $permission }” runs without “Has permission?” checking the command author first.
problem-anyone-can-click = Warning: anyone who clicks can make an action that needs “{ $permission }” run. Tick “Only the user who started it can click” on the message.
problem-option-name = Option { $option }: the name needs 1–32 lower-case letters, digits, - or _.
problem-option-duplicate = Option { $option }: another option has the same name.
problem-option-description = Option { $option }: the description needs 1–100 characters.
problem-option-type = Option { $option } cannot have this type.
problem-option-order = Option { $option } is required, so it must come before the optional ones.
problem-option-too-many = A command can have at most 25 options.
problem-button-label = Button { $item }: the label needs 1–80 characters.
problem-button-url = Button { $item }: a link needs an address starting with https://.
problem-button-id = Button { $item } has a broken ID; remove it and add it again.
problem-menu-label = Menu option { $item }: the label needs 1–100 characters.
problem-menu-id = Menu option { $item } has a broken ID; remove it and add it again.
problem-component-too-many = A message has at most 5 buttons and 25 menu options.
problem-only-author-without-user = “Only the user who started it can click” needs a user, and this event has none.
problem-no-event-message = “The event's message” works only in “New message” and reactions; choose “Last sent by the bot”.
problem-unknown-memory = No memory variable “{ $name }”: add it under Memory in the project tree.
problem-memory-needs-server = This variable is kept per server, and nothing here comes from a server.
problem-memory-needs-user = This variable is kept per user, and no user is known here: choose one.
problem-memory-not-number = “Change by” works only on a number variable.
problem-not-a-number = The field “{ $prop }” must be a number, or a variable.

